  1888	      // (reconciler.ts). So this early return leaves the batch row resting in
  1889	      // its pre-submit status while its constituent anchors are settled by the
  1890	      // reconciler, and the two can diverge indefinitely. That is the RIGHT
  1891	      // trade — a stranded batch row beats terminally failing every anchor in a
  1892	      // batch whose transaction is on chain — and the settling half is KS-774,
  1893	      // filed under KS-489. Peter's finding on #764, carried intact.
  1894	      if (batchWrittenAheadTxHash && REAL_TX_64HEX_RETRY.test(batchWrittenAheadTxHash)) {
